  "name": "Question 9",
  "problem": "What is the linear transformation $T$ whose standard matrix is $T=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]?$\n\n  \n\n| $T:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-2}} |  |  |",
  "worked_solution": "Consider a general vector $\\,[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}].$ Multiplying by the matrix $T,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 5 \\\\ -2 & 7\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}5y \\\\ -2x+7y\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the linear transformation $\\,T\\,$ is given by\n\n$$\nT:[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]\u27f6[\\begin{aligned}5y \\\\ -2x+7y\\end{aligned}].\n$$",
